Exactly—same deep mechanism, different vector.

Evoke = call something forth from within: a memory, feeling, image, state, association.
Provoke = call something forth by applying a stimulus: a reaction, response, confrontation, thought, action.

Both come through Latin vocare — “to call.”

* e-voke → call out
* pro-voke → call forth / forward

So you can frame the pattern as:

stimulus → latent potential → expression

The stimulus can evoke what was already waiting in the system, or provoke the system strongly enough that it produces a response.

And that gives you a larger family: invoke = call upon/into operation; revoke = call back; convoke = call together.

Same operator—calling—with the prefix changing the geometry of the call.